src/core/maint_sched_pg.c	WaitLatch(MyLatch, WL_LATCH_SET | WL_TIMEOUT	the naptime of the launcher and of the workers of the queue: a request sets their latch, the timeout is the periodic reap of the claims of dead processes and the count of idle naps that ends a worker
src/agg/gpu_worker.c	WL_EXIT_ON_PM_DEATH, 1000, PG_WAIT_EXTENSION	the idle look of the GPU worker: a backend that posts a job sets its latch, the second bounds the idle exit (SIFT_GPU_IDLE_US) and keeps the heartbeat the waiting backends read
src/agg/gpu_worker.c	WL_EXIT_ON_PM_DEATH, WAIT_SLICE_MS, PG_WAIT_EXTENSION	a backend waiting for the GPU worker (to start, for a slot, for its job): the party that changes the slot sets the latch, the slice lets the waiter see a worker that died or stopped beating, which sets no latch
src/core/maint_drain.c	WaitLatch(MyLatch, WL_LATCH_SET | WL_TIMEOUT	a statement that drops or copies a database waits at most 5 s for its workers to leave: nothing announces the exit of another process, the server polls the same way (CountOtherDBBackends)
